AB  - This work aims to design artificial intelligence systems used for medical purposes, including diagnosis of corneal surface conditions using Zernike coefficients. In this work, use 135 case studies of patients that 80 females and 55 males were collected, 32 of which were abnormal and 103 were normal, the orange program was used to design five theories of artificial intelligence, the Neural Network, Tree, Logistic regression, KNN, ADABOOST use 10 non-defined samples were used for the purpose of normal or abnormal diagnosis The sample information was entered into CSV formats where it was used for the purpose of training the theories used, the Tree results showed 100% of the expected results Neural Network gave results of 100% of the expected results, while the Logistic regression Research theory gave results of 50% of the expected results and the KNN theory gave results of 70% of the expected results and ADABOOST theory gave results of 100% of expected results. These theories were tested by repeating the number of samples used to 616 samples and applied to 10 unknown samples concluded that there were theories that increased accuracy in diagnosis such as tree theories and changed the percentage of expected results from 70% to 100% like the theory of KNN, the rest of the theories did not change the rates of diagnosis and also did not change the proportion of expected results.
